  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Host and Rohingya Enhancement of Lives Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The developmental object of the Bangladesh - Host and Rohingya Enhancement of Lives Project is to improve access to basic services and enhance disaster and climate resilience of the Host Communities and Displaced Rohingya Population (DRP). The project will consist of the following components - Component 1: Resilient Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH) (US$105 million &#x2013; US$55 million credit and US$50 million grant); Component 2: Climate and Disaster Resilient Infrastructure, Energy and Emergency Response (US$220 million &#x2013; US$145
million credit and US$75 million grant); Component 3: Strengthening Institutional Systems to Enhance Service Provision and Support Resilient Development (US$25 million &#x2013; US$15 million credit and US$10 million grant); and Component 4: Contingent Emergency Response (US$0 million).</narrative>
  </description>
